
# Firebase Configuration - CareerCopilot
#
# All Firebase secrets must be set via environment variables and never committed to source control.
#
# Example (do not commit real values):
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-api-key-here
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project-id.firebaseapp.com
# VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
# VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project-id.appspot.com
# VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your-messaging-sender-id
# VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your-app-id

# ========================================
# IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTES:
# ========================================
# 1. Never commit .env files with real credentials to version control
# 2. Use different Firebase projects for development/staging/production
# 3. Configure Firebase security rules to restrict data access
# 4. Set up proper authentication and authorization
# 5. Monitor Firebase usage and set up billing alerts
# ========================================